WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
[Soft instrumental music]
What if your next onboarding guide

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.840
became something people could actually
practise?

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.840
Turn an idea into a hands-on GitHub
exercise

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.920
with GitHub Copilot and the
gh-skills-builder plugin.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.320
For educators, maintainers, enterprises,
startups, and internal training,

6
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.790
this workshop puts you in the architect's
seat. Copilot helps draft the content and

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.640
scaffold the files. You shape the learning
experience.

8
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.160
One orchestrator agent and five reusable
skills guide the journey.

9
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.880
Outline, bootstrap, review, publish, and
orchestrate the whole loop.

10
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.760
Install the plugin from the
awesome-copilot marketplace

11
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.160
in the Copilot app or CLI. Start with the
outcome.

12
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.560
Define what learners will practise, what
success looks like, and how to check it.

13
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.780
Then turn the approved outline into a
runnable, issue-driven GitHub

14
00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.960
Skills exercise. The example uses Tailspin
Toys

15
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.620
to teach three practical Copilot habits.
Clear repository instructions,

16
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.180
consistent quality reports, and a
report-only QA agent.

17
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:11.020
A small exercise with a concrete purpose,
checks examine what learners wrote,

18
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:16.800
not just whether a file exists. Review the
findings, approve a targeted fix,

19
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.160
and review again. Useful feedback helps
learners understand

20
00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.800
what to improve. People stay in control of
the decisions.

21
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.780
Prepare the validation evidence and launch
checklist, then pause.

22
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.440
Release readiness is not permission to
publish,

23
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:37.480
and this workshop stops before public
release. Watch the live walkthrough,

24
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:42.160
then replay the copyable prompts at your
own pace. The website brings the slides,

25
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.210
instructions and resources together,
repeatable, observable, inclusive, and

26
00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.720
human-led. Explore the workshop, get the
plugin, and bring your next idea.

27
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.710
Build a learning experience people can put
into practice.

28
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.000
[Instrumental music fades]

